<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Albany Intl cut to neutral.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Albany Intl cut to neutral.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Lehman Brothers said it downgraded Albany International Corp to neutral from outperform.</p>
<p>-- Said was &quot;very pleased&quot; with company's Q1 1997 margins and EPS, but cut 1997 and 1998 year estimates by $0.10 each, citing soft second quarter paper production outlook and weakness in Asia.</p>
<p>-- New 12-18 month price target is $23 per share or 12-times 1998 EPS estimate of $1.95, down from $29 or 14-times old estimate of $2.05.</p>
<p>-- Shares fell 1/4 to 20-1/4.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
